pySMESH: Cartesian_3D with viscous layers frees its offset mesh (SMESH V9_16_0; applies after
StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL_cancel.patch).

Defect: StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D::Compute with a ViscousLayers hypothesis makes the offset mesh
with `new TmpMesh()` (StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx:156) and frees it on no path: not on the two
early returns (:161, :164), not after MakeViscousLayers.

Symptom: the working set grows with every compute of a solid with viscous layers.

Change, in StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx only: the offset mesh is held by a std::unique_ptr, so
every return frees it.

Not changed: what is meshed.
diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 
 //STD
 #include <limits>
+#include <memory>
 #include <thread>
 
 // BOOST
@@ -155,7 +156,8 @@
     if ( _computeCanceled ) // pySMESH: canceled during the offset step
       return false;
 
-    SMESH_Mesh* offsetMesh = new TmpMesh(); 
+    // pySMESH: owned here, so every return frees it (it leaked on all of them)
+    std::unique_ptr< SMESH_Mesh > offsetMesh( new TmpMesh() );
     offsetMesh->ShapeToMesh( offsetShape );
     offsetMesh->GetSubMesh( offsetShape )->DependsOn();
 
